{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If the length of data is not a multiple of size, the final partial chunk is yielded.\n    If size is larger than the length of data, a single chunk containing all data is yielded.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or list): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        bytes or list: Chunks of data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Chunk size must be positive\")\n    if not data:\n        return\n    # Always yield chunks in steps of size, including the last partial chunk\n    for i in range(0, len(data), size):\n        yield data[i:i + size]\n","expected_sha256":"d31e937a070d294473410f436d844740e358801861f120de80015d4747751277","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Removed the special case that yielded data once if size >= len(data) to ensure the final partial chunk is always yielded, including when size is larger than data length. Also added a check to raise ValueError for non-positive chunk sizes, and return immediately if data is empty, preserving the public API and fixing the test failures."}